    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **70 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, 0 skipped.**\n\n## Summary\n\nI released version 2 of the owner identity. The V2 version tag now mixes only *inside* the identifiers, while user-facing region fields stay plain.\n\n**Identity derivation (V2 tag mixed in, so every identifier changes and no V1 value recurs):**\n- `mapper/IdentityKeys.java` \u2014 added a `VERSION_TAG = \"V2\"` constant and prefixed the identity-key SHA-256 input with it. Still a 64-hex SHA-256 (Cp28), and duplicate detection stays consistent because both sides hash the same way (Cp03, Cp46).\n- `controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java` \u2014 `householdId(...)` now folds `V2` into its SHA-256 input; `memberId` now uses a new `deriveRegionV2(...)` (plain region with the `V2` tag prefixed, e.g. `NSW` \u2192 `V2NSW`), used **only** inside the member id.\n\n**User-facing fields unchanged:** `locality` stays `NSW`, `timezone` and the owner segment's derived region use the plain `deriveRegion`/`locality`, so `ownerSegment` stays `STANDARD_METRO` (Cp17, Cp30, Cp42, Cp55).\n\n**Response shape (`openapi.yml` + `mapper/OwnerMapper.java`):**\n- New `OwnerIdentity` schema grouping `memberId`, `identityKey`, `householdId`; these are removed from the top level.\n- Added top-level integer `apiVersion` = 2, and an `identity` object built by a new `identity(owner)` mapper method (Cp11, Cp28, Cp32, Cp36, Cp41, Cp52, Cp56, Cp57, Cp60).\n\n**Audit schema:** the machine-readable `OWNER_CREATED` event now carries `\"schemaVersion\": 2` and an `ownerSegment` recomputed from the (V2) saved owner via the mapper (Cp53), and the NOTIFY/human audit lines still carry the id and V2 memberId.\n\nRequest fields are untouched.",
