    "probe_text": "This is handled by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java:151`), which implements the generated `OwnersApi` for `POST /api/owners`. Here is everything it does, in execution order.\n\n## Pre-check (before any validation)\n\n1. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` gates the whole call.\n2. **Idempotency short-circuit** \u2014 read the `Idempotency-Key` header; if it's non-blank and already recorded from a prior successful create, return that stored owner with **200 OK** and do nothing else (no new owner, no side-effects).\n\n## Validations (in order; each rejects the request)\n\n3. **Address normalization** \u2014 normalize `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` (structured, preferred) or the flat `address`; trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST/RD/AVE`. This composed value feeds the required-field check below.\n4. **Required fields** \u2014 collect any blank among `firstName`, `lastName`, the normalized `address`, `city`, `telephone`; if any are missing \u2192 `InvalidOwnerFieldsException` (**400**).\n5. **Future registration date** \u2014 if a `registrationDate` is supplied and is after `LocalDate.now()` (checked against the raw value, today = 2026-08-11) \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException` (**400**).\n6. **Daily owner limit** \u2014 compute the effective registration date (supplied-or-today, rolled forward to a business day skipping weekends and the fixed 2026 holidays); if \u2265 **100** owners already carry that date \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitExceededException` (**429**).\n7. **City capacity** \u2014 if the city (case-insensitive) already holds \u2265 **50** owners \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` (**409**).\n8. **Postcode** \u2014 optional; if present it must be exactly 4 digits and, when the city maps to a known region (Sydney\u2192NSW, Melbourne\u2192VIC, Brisbane\u2192QLD), fall within that region's range \u2192 else `InvalidOwnerFieldsException` (**400**).\n9. **Telephone E.164** \u2014 strip spaces/dashes/brackets, assume `+61` if no country code (dropping one leading `0`); result must be `+` and 8\u201315 digits, with the correct national length for `+61` (9) / `+1` (10) \u2192 else `InvalidOwnerFieldsException` (**400**).\n10. **Email** \u2014 optional; if present must match the email pattern and not be a disposable domain (mailinator/tempmail/guerrillamail) \u2192 else `InvalidOwnerFieldsException` (**400**); stored lower-cased.\n11. **Duplicate identity** \u2014 build the SHA-256 identity key over `normalizedTelephone | lowerEmail | soundex(lastName)`; if any existing non-deleted owner has the same key \u2192 `DuplicateOwnerIdentityException` (**409**).\n\n## Side-effects (once all validations pass)\n\nComputed and stamped onto the new `Owner`:\n\n12. **address** = composed normalized address; **addressLine1/addressLine2** retained only for structured input (else null).\n13. **telephone** = E.164 form; **email** = normalized lower-cased.\n14. **householdId** = deterministic SHA-256-derived id from normalized last name + postcode.\n15. **namesakeCount** = existing owners sharing first+last name (case-insensitive), excluding the new one.\n16. **householdSize** = existing household members + 1.\n17. **membershipLevelCap** = `null` if `sharesHousehold`, else one above the max membership level among existing household members.\n18. **bulkSignupWarning** = true if > **80** owners already registered that business day.\n19. **capacityWarning** = true if the city already holds 40\u201349 owners.\n20. **registrationDate** = the business-day-adjusted effective date.\n21. **memberId** = `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>` (V2 region, fiscal-year, SHA-256 hash, Luhn digit), de-duplicated with a `-<n>` suffix on collision.\n22. **possibleDuplicate / possibleDuplicateOf** = soft-match flag (same soundex(lastName) + postcode but different identity key); skipped (null) when `sharesHousehold`.\n\nThen:\n\n23. **Persist** \u2014 `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` writes the row (assigns the id).\n24. **Audit log** \u2014 `AUDIT` logger emits a human-readable `owner created \u2026` line.\n25. **Structured audit event** \u2014 `AUDIT` logger emits a JSON `OWNER_CREATED` event (schemaVersion 2, incremented `AUDIT_EVENT_SEQ`, ownerId, memberId, membershipLevel, ownerSegment).\n26. **Notification** \u2014 `NOTIFY` logger emits a `welcome owner \u2026` line.\n27. **Location header** \u2014 set to `/api/owners/{id}`.\n28. **Record idempotency key** \u2014 if an `Idempotency-Key` was supplied, store the response DTO under it for future replays.\n29. **Return 201 CREATED** with the owner DTO.\n\nOne thing worth flagging: the `updateOwner` path (`PUT`) applies almost none of this \u2014 it only runs `toE164`/`normalizeEmail`, so the two endpoints diverge significantly in what they enforce."
